Section Explanations:

1. Top Navigation Bar
   - Visible on all pages, it offers primary navigation: “Dashboard”, “Appointments”, “Search”, “Settings”.
   - Ensures recognizable and consistent access to core features.

2. Left Sub-Menu (Contextual)
   - Appears when user is in “Appointments”; provides quick filters (Upcoming, Past, All) for easy segmentation/navigation.
   - Each item is clickable and updates the list in main content.

3. Main Content Area
   - Top: Dashboard summary (quick stats: total appointments, next appointment, etc.), aids status visibility.
   - Below: Week navigator (e.g., “< Prev | Jun 10-16 | >”) to quick-browse appointment weeks.
   - Center: Appointment list in table/list format. Shows time, client, with Edit/Delete icons per row.
   - Prominent “+ New Appointment” button for primary CTA.
   - Action buttons (Edit, Delete) next to each appointment for quick management.

4. Fixed Footer
   - Persistent, includes quick links: help, privacy, contact, copyright.
   - Provides support and legal access from any page.

Navigation & Interactions:
- Top nav enables jumping between application modules; left nav filters entities.
- User sees immediate system status (upcoming/past appointments, quick summary).
- Primary work focus and attention: main appointment list and booking (“+ New Appointment”).
- All actions (create, edit, delete) clearly available with visuals (button, icon).
- Users can quickly browse through weeks and filter appointment types.

