Section Explanations:

1. Top Navigation Bar
   - Consistently visible for accessing “Dashboard”, “Appointments”, “Patients”, “Search”, and “Settings”.
   - “Clinic Logo” always links home (dashboard).

2. Left Sub-Menu (Contextual)
   - Visible on “Appointments”.
   - Filters for Upcoming, Past, Cancelled, All appointments.
   - Clicking changes main list instantly for focused workflows.

3. Main Content Area
   - Dashboard Overview: Summarizes today’s appointments and next up.
   - Date Navigation: Users move by days via Prev/Next for at-a-glance scheduling.
   - Appointment List Table: Standard columns (Time, Patient, Provider, Status, Row Actions).
   - Actions: [View], [Edit], [Del] let users manage appointments rapidly.
   - [+ New Appointment] is primary CTA, always visible below table. “Bulk Actions” for advanced operations (e.g., mass-cancel, reschedule).
   - Space and grouping keep scanning/management clean and fast.

4. Fixed Footer
   - Accessible support, policy, and contact links on every screen.
   - Persistent, doesn’t distract from main workflow.

Navigation & Interactions:
- Top nav for module switching. Left sub-menu for focused lists inside Appointments.
- Overview clearly states entity count (e.g., how many appointments today).
- Date navigation encourages easy browsing.
- All appointment management actions explicit and visible—no hidden controls.
- Prominent action button drives primary use: quick appointment creation.

