Section Explanations:

1. Top Navigation Bar
   - Central access to “Dashboard”, “Properties”, “Tenants”, “Work Orders”, “Settings”.
   - “AssetPro Logo” always links home (dashboard).

2. Left Sub-Menu (Contextual)
   - Visible on “Properties”.
   - Filters: All Properties, Vacant, Occupied, Maintenance.
   - Selecting a filter updates the property list for focused management.

3. Main Content Area
   - Dashboard Overview: Quick stats (e.g., total properties, vacant count, open work orders).
   - Quick Navigation: Month selector (Prev/Next) for viewing metrics/entries by time.
   - Properties Table: Shows Name, Address, Status (Occupied/Vacant/Maint.), Tenant, Actions.
   - Actions: [View] always available. [Edit] for editable entities. [Delete] only for appropriate records (not shown here to reduce accidental deletions).
   - [+ Add Property] is the prominent CTA. “Bulk Actions” for mass edit, export, etc.

4. Fixed Footer
   - Help, Privacy, Contact links always available for support and legal info.

Navigation & Interactions:
- Top bar is global module switching; left sub-menu aids detailed property filtering.
- Dashboard overview and table spotlight primary system status and tasks.
- Quick navigation lets users switch time periods if relevant.
- All management actions are surfaced as explicit buttons for clarity.
- Main actions (“+ Add Property”) are prominent, driving efficient workflows.

Delegating to coding agent for UI implementation."
